From Cinder's README, at the pinned commit:

The efficiently updatable neural networks (NNUE) Cinder uses for position evaluation are
trained with bullet (https://github.com/jw1912/bullet), by Jamie Whiting
(https://github.com/jw1912), using data generated by the Leela Chess Zero project
(https://lczero.org/), which is available under the Open Database License (ODbL)
(https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/).
